# The inherited curriculum is hash-locked, so its bytes must survive a
# checkout unchanged. Without this, git rewrites line endings on Windows and a
# fresh clone fails `npm run content:check` having changed nothing -- the lock
# reporting a "difference" that is only a checkout artefact.
#
# scripts/sync-upstream.mjs also normalises line endings before hashing every
# text form the curriculum uses. Both, deliberately: the normaliser keeps an
# existing clone honest, and this keeps the working tree byte-exact.
upstream/** -text
